{"ts":"2026-08-24T08:36:24.529Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"stealth/ox-alpha","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"074ac6c6e28b52727548416c","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"stealth/ox-alpha","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-24T08:36:24.529Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-24T08:36:24.529Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"CodeRabbit PR #79 thread 3836774695 resolved with real evidence instead of a live release run: the alert step's inline script was extracted verbatim into scripts/alert-on-release-failure.sh and the workflow job now checks out the repo and runs it, so workflow and tests execute the same bytes. New hermetic suite test/alert-on-release-failure.test.ts stubs gh on PATH and proves all three behaviours the YAML verifier could not: single create with release-failure label + stable title + run URL/commit/date body; comment-on-existing-#77 deduplication without a second create; and exit 0 plus ::warning:: when every gh call fails. Mutation proof: with the dedup lookup broken (existing_number emptied), the suite fails 3/4 tests; restored, 4/4 pass. shellcheck v0.10.0 clean; npm test 274 pass; coverage thresholds met (100 lines/92.15 branches/100 functions); pm health --strict-exit green; changelog:full+check green."}]}],"before_hash":"7267d9d25e9e8daaf526a34124587305d9bd5997352ae55ac3a6c953620f767d","after_hash":"93363cf613cc35a25cb726fbc4f6fe54ea11d702bfddadaa2ceff2ec6419281f","item_hash_version":2}
